  "term": "anaphylaxis",
  "definition": "Anaphylaxis is a severe, sudden inflammatory reaction in which mast cells release histamine and similar substances, triggering a hypersensitivity immune response. It can cause trouble breathing, dizziness, low blood pressure, bluish skin color, and loss of consciousness, and it may be fatal.",
